ill not be sudden it will be gradual  as our plan is in ontario phased  monitored and we want to move up to  around 70 surgical capacity and that is  those that have been waiting for a new  knee a new hip cataract surgeries those  we want to return  gradually without significantly  impacting the system to ensure that we  are able to provide care to in those  regions where there is increased covet  activity and also to provide equity  across ontario  so we will do it in those phased  approaches of around 70 of their  surgical  capacity keeping that availability for  covid patients then move up to around 90  percent surgical capacity and then when  we're in a recovery phase which we  anticipate being in in late march and  april uh opening up surgeries back to  normal normal volumes to uh then try to  also do some catch up on any procedures  that were significantly delayed so i  hope everyone's hearing staged phased  evidence-based cautious approaches  are the mainstay in ontario of how to  return the health system back to  recovery  thanks everyone
 

